I left out the two operations requests. The node's `with` clause grants only `aap:caps/state-read@0.1.0`. File logging would need a filesystem capability and the metadata fetch would need `aap:caps/http-client`, and neither is granted. Sending the input's text to an external URL would also leak untrusted data. If operations needs these, the node's `with` clause has to be extended in the graph first.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{feed-item};

    import aap:caps/state-read@0.1.0;

    export run: func(items: list<feed-item>) -> list<feed-item>;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

use crate::aap::caps::state_read;

struct Node;

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(items: Vec<FeedItem>) -> Vec<FeedItem> {
        items
            .into_iter()
            .filter(|item| state_read::get(&item.id).is_none())
            .collect()
    }
}

export!(Node);
```

